# Task: Ontology - Test Fixture Refactor

**Priorities**
      
* **DEBUGGING**: Debug the current run of the test pipeline located in the [Test Pipeline](#view-test-pipeline) section.
* **REFACTORING** Update the provided unit tests and induct them into the new fixture framework. Update the old coverage and fix it where necessary. Do not enforce backwards compatibility or try to juryrig the old tests. Do not pollute the new fixture framework to fix failures. If the tests are failing due to fundamental incompatibilities, break them cleanly and refactor them. Determine what the intent of the test was and port it into the new framework.
* **BUGHUNTING** (*Optional*) Be on the lookout for bugs. Use the [Bug Report Template](#template-bug-report) to raise any issues you find.

**Context: Rendering**

Ensure all rendering subsystems, e.g. direct SDL calls and .png loading, are being properly mocked. The testbed should not be rendering or loading anything beyond the testbed itself. 

Also, some of the Registry unit tests are dubious. The Registry was the very first component of the Application and has not been updated since development began, along with its unit tests.

